WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.230
The document is open. Alex has even

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:05.630
chosen a font. So why hasn't he

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:06.090
started?

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:09.660
He reaches for his phone. For a

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.780
moment, the uncomfortable task disappears.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.870
That relief is real. The deadline is

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:19.390
also real. It is now closer.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.160
Sometimes postponing a task is a way

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.720
to postpone how it feels.

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:29.670
But not every delay is avoidance. Missing

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:33.070
information, exhaustion, and conflicting priorities can matter

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:33.410
too.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:36.980
Alex asks a smaller question: what can

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:38.440
I do before I feel ready?

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:43.750
He writes one rough sentence. It isn't

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:46.090
good yet. Now there is something to

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:46.410
improve.
